**Forward square DCT-DCT gets a `_v4` tier — the largest remaining mapped
C-AVX-512 gap, and the campaign's biggest single win so far.** Fourth
target. C registers `svt_av1_fwd_txfm2d_{16x16,32x32,64x64}` (+ rect/N2/N4
sizes) at AVX-512; the port had only the `_v3` x8 lane group. Callgrind
priced `fdct64_x8`/`fdct32_x8`/`try_fwd_dct_square_impl_v3` at ~12–29M self
Ir combined per inter cell (valgrind masks AVX-512 — the `_v3` arm's cost).

date:   2026-09-19
host:   r7900x — AMD Ryzen 9 7900X, **Zen 4: AVX-512 double-pumped over
        256-bit units**. perf_event_paranoid=4 — wall clock only.
base:   `70e348cfa` — convolve _sr _v4 commit.
cand:   working tree — `crates/svtav1-dsp/src/txfm_simd.rs` +
        `txfm_simd_kernels_v4.rs` + `txfm_simd_drivers_v4.rs` (new).
data:   benchmarks/txfm_fwd_square_avx512_inter_grad.ab.{tsv,raw.tsv} (32r)
        benchmarks/txfm_fwd_square_avx512_still_grad.ab.{tsv,raw.tsv} (24r)

========================= 1. WHAT LANDS =========================

A `mod v4` (x86_64 + avx512) inside `txfm_simd.rs` with zmm twins of the
v3 primitives (`splat`/`hbtf`/`round_shift_v`/`load16`/`load16w`/`store16`),
plus:

- `txfm_simd_kernels_v4.rs`: `fdct16_x16`, `fdct32_x16`, `fdct64_x16` —
  mechanically widened copies of the `_x8` kernels (`__m256i`→`__m512i`,
  `_mm256_*`→`_mm512_*`). The butterflies are purely lanewise (each lane is
  an independent column), so identical op order keeps bit-exactness. The
  i32 `mullo` range argument carries over unchanged (lane width doesn't
  affect it).
- `txfm_simd_drivers_v4.rs`: `fwd_dct_{16,32,64}` — column pass is
  contiguous 16-col zmm work; the row pass uses `transpose16`, built from
  four quadrant 8x8 `ymm` transposes (the proven `transpose8` sequence) —
  pure data movement.
- `try_fwd_dct_square_impl_v4` + `v4` in the `try_fwd_dct_square` incant.
  `n == 8` delegates to `v3::fwd_dct_square` (8 columns don't fill a zmm);
  a bare `false` there would have dropped 8x8 to scalar — a regression.
- Inverse, rect, ADST, ext paths stay on `v3` (follow-up scope).

========================= 2. RESULTS (Zen 4, wall clock) =========================

Interleaved paired A/B, `tools/perf_ab.sh`, gradient 512²; `ident=Y`
everywhere.

  inter p6 (32r): 0.9818 [0.9761, 0.9882]   — disjoint, ~1.8%
  inter p8 (32r): 0.9827 [0.9756, 0.9851]   — disjoint, ~1.7%
  still p6 (24r): 0.9829 [0.9709, 0.9915]   — disjoint, ~1.7%
  still p8 (24r): 0.9825 [0.9704, 0.9884]   — disjoint, ~1.8%

  (inter cell: SVTAV1_FRAMES=4 FRAME_SHIFT=3 INTRA_PERIOD=64
   HIER_LEVELS=0 INTER_EXPERIMENTAL=1)

Zen-4-specific numbers; full-width 512-bit silicon unmeasured.

========================= 3. GATES =========================

- `cargo nextest run -p zenav1-svt-dsp --locked` txfm suite: 58/58
  (c_parity_txfm*, real-C differentials across sizes/tiers).
- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked --test-threads 4`: 3930/3930.
- `tools/regression_spotcheck.sh`: 145/145.
- Decode gate NOT run (no dav1d) — known coverage gap.

========================= 4. REMAINING MAPPED GAPS =========================

- Same machinery applied to: inv square/rect DCT (C has
  `inv_txfm2d_add_{16x16..64x64}` at AVX-512), fwd rect (reuses the `_x16`
  kernels + a zmm `rect_scale`), ADST/ext.
- `jnt_convolve_{x,y,2d}`, `convolve_2d_copy_sr` (C AVX-512, cooler cells).
- `svt_residual_kernel8bit`, `svt_spatial_full_distortion_kernel`,
  `svt_av1_compute_stats`, `svt_av1_lowbd_pixel_proj_error`,
  `svt_av1_txb_init_levels` — check shares.
